This README file contains a brief description of the verification case.

A simple test for a 1-d spherical case with only 100 elements. To test the function
of OFFBEAT of calculating the mechanics with transversely isotropic thermal expansion.

The equation for constant temperature and thermal expansion coefficient can be expressed as:
d²u/dr² + 2/r*du/dr - 2u/r² = 2(1-2nu)/(1-nu)/r*(alpha_r-alpha_theta)*deltaT;

For a solid sphere with free expansion (no pressure outside the sphere)
the analytical solution is:
u = A/3*r*ln(r)+B*r
A = 2(1-2nu)/(1-v)*(alpha_r-alpha_theta)*deltaT;
B = (alpha_r+2*alpha_theta)/3*deltaT - A/3*ln(a);
a is the radius of the sphere.

The BAF was set to = 1.5 (which normally is not correct, but the object is to have a very different
coef along r and theta direction), so
alpha_r = 8.84101836734694E-06
alpha_theta = 4.06265844023324E-06

Other parameters can be found in the file compare.ods with the verification results.
